-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA), 07-a0-00, Part V: the provisions by which a tenancy ends and the
-- next begins: s 60 (Division 1), ss 64, 65, 70A and 70 (Division 2) and s 76C (Division 5), with r 7D.
-- Source: sources/rta-1987.07-a0-00.mrdoc_49316.txt lines 1411-1434 (s 60), 1470-1489 (ss 64-65),
-- 1513-1534 (ss 70A, 70), 1815-1819 (s 76C). Reference register REF-15, -22, -43, -52, -55, -66,
-- -67, -68, -75 (encoded links); REF-53, -54, -56 to -65, -69, -70, -74, -76 (facts).
-- Termination on grounds, court orders under ss 71-75 and abandonment are facts: they enter s 60
-- as circumstances with the day they take effect.
-- LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`
IMPORT `regulations-1989`
IMPORT `part-3-div-3-retaliatory-action`

§ `Section 70A -- Notice of termination by lessor or tenant at end of fixed term tenancy`

-- s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D: "The notice must be given not later than 30 days before the possession
-- day." The 30th day before the possession day p is p - 30 (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(c): the time
-- before a day does not include that day). FK-08, reading taken (A): Interpretation Act s 61(1)(h)
-- applies, so if p - 30 is an excluded day the notice is in time on the next day that is not.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(3); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7D; Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(c), (h); fork FK-08 reading A
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice under s 70A`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 70A(3) -- the last day for giving the notice` n `under` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `the last day for a thing due on day` (n's `possession day specified` MINUS `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` a) `, given the holidays` holidays

-- FK-08, reading rejected (B): s 70A(3) shows a contrary intention, so s 61(1)(h) does not move the
-- last day: it is p - 30 (or p - 7 under r 7D) whatever day of the week that is.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(3); fork FK-08 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 70A`, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`FK-08 reading B -- s 70A(3) -- the last day for giving the notice` n `under` a MEANS
    n's `possession day specified` MINUS `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` a

-- s 70A(3), (4) and (1) "agreement": a notice is a notice under s 70A only for a fixed-term agreement,
-- given in time, with a possession day not earlier than the expiry day. FK-07, reading taken (A): a
-- notice that fails (3) or (4) is not a notice under s 70A at all, and so does not end the term.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(1), (3), (4); fork FK-07 reading A
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice under s 70A`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 70A -- the notice` n `is a notice under the section for` a `, given the holidays` holidays IF
        "agreement means a residential tenancy agreement that creates a tenancy for a fixed term"
    ... a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND "(3) The notice must be given not later than 30 days before the possession day"
    ... n's `given on` AT MOST `s 70A(3) -- the last day for giving the notice` n `under` a `, given the holidays` holidays
    AND "(4) The possession day must not be a day earlier than the expiry day"
    ... (CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST e THEN n's `possession day specified` AT LEAST e)

-- FK-07, reading rejected (B): a notice given late still operates, with its possession day put back to
-- the first day for which it would have been in time (here, the given day plus 30 or 7 days).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(3); fork FK-07 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 70A`, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`FK-07 reading B -- s 70A(3) -- the possession day of a late notice` n `under` a MEANS
    `the later of day` (n's `possession day specified`) `and day` (n's `given on` PLUS `s 70A(3), as modified by r 7D where it applies -- the number of days` a)

-- s 70A(6): "If both the lessor and tenant give a notice to each other and the notices specify different
-- possession days, then the day that is the earlier of the 2 days is to be taken to be the possession
-- day." The earliest possession day among the notices that are notices under s 70A, and who gave it.
DECLARE `Possession day under s 70A` HAS
    `falls on` IS A NUMBER
    `given by` IS A `Party`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(1) "possession day", (6)
GIVEN ns       IS A LIST OF `Notice under s 70A`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Possession day under s 70A`
`the earliest possession day among` ns `for` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER ns
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN n FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `s 70A -- the notice` n `is a notice under the section for` a `, given the holidays` holidays
        THEN CONSIDER `the earliest possession day among` rest `for` a `, given the holidays` holidays
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`Possession day under s 70A` WITH `falls on` IS n's `possession day specified`, `given by` IS n's `given by`)
             WHEN JUST p THEN
                 IF n's `possession day specified` LESS THAN p's `falls on`
                 THEN JUST (`Possession day under s 70A` WITH `falls on` IS n's `possession day specified`, `given by` IS n's `given by`)
                 ELSE JUST p
        ELSE `the earliest possession day among` rest `for` a `, given the holidays` holidays

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(1) "possession day", (6)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Possession day under s 70A`
`s 70A(6) -- the possession day for` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `the earliest possession day among` (a's `notices under s 70A`) `for` a `, given the holidays` holidays

-- s 70A(7): if the term is to expire under (5)(a) on the possession day under the lessor's notice, and
-- the tenant delivers up possession after the expiry day but before that day, the day of delivery is
-- taken to be the possession day for (5).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(5), (6), (7)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 70A(7) -- the possession day for` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 70A(6) -- the possession day for` a `, given the holidays` holidays
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (p's `falls on`)
        WHEN JUST e THEN
            CONSIDER a's `possession delivered up on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (p's `falls on`)
            WHEN JUST v THEN
                IF     p's `given by` EQUALS `the lessor`
                   AND p's `falls on` GREATER THAN e
                   AND v GREATER THAN e
                   AND v LESS THAN p's `falls on`
                THEN JUST v
                ELSE JUST (p's `falls on`)

-- s 70A(2), (5)(a): the term ends on the expiry day only if a notice under s 70A was given; if the
-- possession day is later, the term expires on the possession day. With no notice, the term does not
-- end on the expiry day (and s 76C continues the agreement): the result is then nothing.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(2), (5)(a)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 70A -- the day the term of` a `ends under the section, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `s 70A(7) -- the possession day for` a `, given the holidays` holidays

§ `The last day of a fixed term, and the currency of the term`

-- The fixed term runs from the day the tenancy commences. Its last day is the day the agreement
-- terminated, if it terminated before the expiry day; otherwise the possession day under s 70A where a
-- notice moved it (s 70A(5)); otherwise the expiry day, after which s 76C continues the agreement as a
-- periodic tenancy. FK-10, reading taken (A): where s 70A(5) applies, the fixed term (and so "the
-- currency of that term" in ss 30(2)(a) and 64(5)) runs to the possession day.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 3 "expiry day", 70A(2), (5), 76C(1); fork FK-10 reading A
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the last day of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF `the day` (a's `terminated on`) `is before day` e
        THEN a's `terminated on`
        ELSE CONSIDER `s 70A -- the day the term of` a `ends under the section, given the holidays` holidays
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST e
             WHEN JUST p THEN JUST p

-- FK-10, reading rejected (B): after the expiry day the agreement is a periodic tenancy under s 76C(2),
-- whatever the possession day; the fixed term ends on the expiry day (or earlier termination).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 76C(2); fork FK-10 reading B
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`FK-10 reading B -- the last day of the fixed term of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF `the day` (a's `terminated on`) `is before day` e THEN a's `terminated on` ELSE JUST e

-- "during the currency of that term" (ss 30(2)(a), 63(4), 64(5), 68(3)).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30(2)(a), 64(5) "during the currency of that term"
GIVEN d        IS A NUMBER
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is day` d `during the currency of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays IF
        a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND d AT LEAST a's `tenancy commenced on`
    AND (CONSIDER `the last day of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST l THEN d AT MOST l)

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30(2)(a), 64(5); fork FK-10 reading B
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-10 reading B -- is day` d `during the currency of the fixed term of` a IF
        a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND d AT LEAST a's `tenancy commenced on`
    AND (CONSIDER `FK-10 reading B -- the last day of the fixed term of` a
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST l THEN d AT MOST l)

§ `Section 76C -- Fixed term tenancies continued as periodic tenancies`

-- s 76C(1): "This section applies to a residential tenancy agreement that creates a tenancy for a fixed
-- term unless the agreement is terminated before the expiry day." FK-09, reading taken (A): the section
-- does not continue an agreement that has terminated by the last day of its fixed term (on the expiry
-- day, or on a later possession day under s 70A(5)); "continues" presupposes an agreement in force.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 76C(1); fork FK-09 reading A
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 76C(1) -- the section applies to` a `, given the holidays` holidays IF
        a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND (CONSIDER `the last day of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST l THEN
             CONSIDER a's `terminated on`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST t THEN t GREATER THAN l)

-- FK-09, reading rejected (B): the words alone: the section applies unless the agreement terminated
-- before the expiry day, so an agreement that terminated on the expiry day, or on a later possession
-- day, is within it.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 76C(1); fork FK-09 reading B
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-09 reading B -- s 76C(1) -- the section applies to` a IF
        a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND (CONSIDER `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST e THEN NOT `the day` (a's `terminated on`) `is before day` e)

-- s 76C(2): the agreement "continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day on the same terms that
-- applied immediately before the expiry day" (subject to a court's modification under (3), a fact).
-- The first day of the periodic tenancy, if the section applies: the day after the last day of the
-- fixed term (FK-10 reading A); the agreement, its parties and its rent are unchanged.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 76C(2); fork FK-10 reading A
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76C(2) -- the first day of the periodic tenancy continuing` a `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    IF `s 76C(1) -- the section applies to` a `, given the holidays` holidays
    THEN CONSIDER `the last day of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST l THEN JUST (l PLUS 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 60 -- How residential tenancy agreements and tenant's interests in agreements are terminated`

-- The circumstances s 60(1) lists, each with the day it happens, and three that it does not list.
-- Whether a notice was given under the Act, whether a court made an order and when it operates,
-- abandonment, merger and so on are facts (REF-53, -54, -56, -60 to -63).
DECLARE `Circumstance said to end an agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a notice of termination under the Act, then vacant possession (s 60(1)(a)(i))` HAS
        `the period of notice required under the Act expires on` IS A NUMBER
        `vacant possession delivered up on`                      IS A NUMBER
    `a notice of termination under the Act, then termination by a court under s 71 (s 60(1)(a)(ii))` HAS
        `the order operates from`                                IS A NUMBER
    `a notice under s 70A, then possession delivered up (s 60(1)(b)(i))` HAS
        `the term expires under s 70A on`                        IS A NUMBER
        `possession delivered up on`                             IS A NUMBER
    `a notice under s 70A, then termination by a court under s 72 (s 60(1)(b)(ii))` HAS
        `the order operates from`                                IS A NUMBER
    `termination by a court under s 73, 74, 75A or 75 (s 60(1)(c))` HAS
        `the order operates from`                                IS A NUMBER
    `a person with superior title becomes entitled to possession (s 60(1)(d))` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `a mortgagee takes possession under the mortgage (s 60(1)(e))` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant abandons the premises (s 60(1)(f))` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `vacant possession under a written agreement to terminate (s 60(1)(g))` HAS
        `vacant possession delivered up on`                      IS A NUMBER
    `merger (s 60(1)(h))` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `every tenant dies (s 60(1)(i))` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `an agreement to terminate, the tenant staying in possession` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `a further agreement between the same parties for the premises, the tenant staying in possession` HAS
        `the further agreement starts on`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the expiry day passing without a notice under s 70A` HAS
        `on`                                                     IS A NUMBER

-- s 60(1): "Despite any Act or law to the contrary, a residential tenancy agreement shall not terminate
-- or be terminated except in one of the following circumstances". The day on which the agreement
-- terminates in a circumstance, or nothing if the circumstance does not terminate it.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 60(1)(a)-(i)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstance said to end an agreement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 60(1) -- the day the agreement terminates in` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a notice of termination under the Act, then vacant possession (s 60(1)(a)(i))` e v THEN
        IF v AT LEAST e THEN JUST v ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a notice of termination under the Act, then termination by a court under s 71 (s 60(1)(a)(ii))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `a notice under s 70A, then possession delivered up (s 60(1)(b)(i))` t v THEN
        IF v AT LEAST t THEN JUST v ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a notice under s 70A, then termination by a court under s 72 (s 60(1)(b)(ii))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `termination by a court under s 73, 74, 75A or 75 (s 60(1)(c))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `a person with superior title becomes entitled to possession (s 60(1)(d))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `a mortgagee takes possession under the mortgage (s 60(1)(e))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `the tenant abandons the premises (s 60(1)(f))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `vacant possession under a written agreement to terminate (s 60(1)(g))` v THEN JUST v
    WHEN `merger (s 60(1)(h))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `every tenant dies (s 60(1)(i))` d THEN JUST d
    WHEN `an agreement to terminate, the tenant staying in possession` d THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a further agreement between the same parties for the premises, the tenant staying in possession` d THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the expiry day passing without a notice under s 70A` d THEN NOTHING

-- s 60(2): "The termination of a tenant's interest in a residential tenancy agreement does not terminate
-- the agreement in respect of any other tenant under the agreement." The tenants who remain.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 60(2)
GIVEN gone IS A STRING
      ts   IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the tenants other than` gone `among` ts MEANS
    CONSIDER ts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN t FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF t EQUALS gone
        THEN `the tenants other than` gone `among` rest
        ELSE t FOLLOWED BY (`the tenants other than` gone `among` rest)

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 60(2)
GIVEN gone IS A STRING, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60(2) -- after the interest of` gone `ends, the agreement continues for another tenant of` a IF
    NOT (`the tenants other than` gone `among` (a's `tenants`) EQUALS EMPTY)

§ `Section 64 -- Notice of termination by lessor without any ground`

DECLARE `Notice under s 64` HAS
    `given on`                 IS A NUMBER
    `received by the tenant on` IS A NUMBER
    `possession day specified` IS A NUMBER

-- s 64(5): "This section does not apply in relation to a residential tenancy agreement that creates a
-- tenancy for a fixed term during the currency of that term." Read at the day the notice is given.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(1), (5)
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice under s 64`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(5) -- the section applies to the notice` n `under` a `, given the holidays` holidays IF
    NOT `is day` (n's `given on`) `during the currency of the fixed term of` a `, given the holidays` holidays

-- s 64(2): "the period of notice must be not less than 60 days before the day on which the tenant is
-- required under the notice to give to the lessor possession of the premises". FK-06, reading taken
-- (A): Interpretation Act s 61(1)(f): "not less than" a number of days between 2 events excludes both
-- days, so 60 clear days must lie between the giving and the possession day.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(2); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(f); fork FK-06 reading A
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(2) -- the period of notice is long enough` n IF
    `the number of clear days between day` (n's `given on`) `and day` (n's `possession day specified`) AT LEAST 60

-- FK-06, reading rejected (B): the possession day need only be the 60th day after the giving (s 61(1)(b)).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(2); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b); fork FK-06 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-06 reading B -- s 64(2) -- the period of notice is long enough` n IF
    n's `possession day specified` AT LEAST `the last day of the period of` 60 `days after day` (n's `given on`)

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(1), (2), (5)
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice under s 64`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64 -- the notice` n `is a notice of termination under the section for` a `, given the holidays` holidays IF
        `s 64(5) -- the section applies to the notice` n `under` a `, given the holidays` holidays
    AND `s 64(2) -- the period of notice is long enough` n

-- s 64(3): the tenant may apply "within 7 days after receiving a notice"; Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b), (e).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(3); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`, holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 64(3) -- the last day for the tenant to apply for an extension of` n `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after day` (n's `received by the tenant on`) `, given the holidays` holidays

-- s 64(4)(a): the court may "extend the period of notice for a further period of up to 60 days".
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(4)(a); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(g)
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(4)(a) -- the court may extend the possession day of` n `to day` d IF
        d AT LEAST n's `possession day specified`
    AND `the number of days from day` (n's `possession day specified`) `to day` d AT MOST 60

-- s 64(4)(c): an order under s 71(2) operates from "a day that is the later of -- (i) a day not less
-- than 60 days after the day on which the notice of termination was received; or (ii) a day within 7
-- days after the day on which the order was made". FK-05, reading taken (A): the court fixes a day
-- within 7 days after the order, and the order operates from that day or, if later, from the first day
-- that is not less than 60 days after receipt (60 clear days, FK-06 A).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(4)(c); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b), (f); fork FK-05 reading A
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`, o IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(4)(c) -- on the notice` n `, an order made on day` o `may operate from day` d IF
        "(i)"  ... d AT LEAST `the first day not less than` 60 `days after day` (n's `received by the tenant on`)
    AND "(ii)" ... d AT LEAST o PLUS 1
    AND "the later of" ... d AT MOST `the later of day` (`the first day not less than` 60 `days after day` (n's `received by the tenant on`)) `and day` (`the last day of the period of` 7 `days after day` o)

-- FK-05, reading rejected (B): the words read literally: the day is the later of any day not less than
-- 60 days after receipt and any day within 7 days after the order, which puts no upper limit on it.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(4)(c); fork FK-05 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice under s 64`, o IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-05 reading B -- s 64(4)(c) -- on the notice` n `, an order made on day` o `may operate from day` d IF
        d AT LEAST `the first day not less than` 60 `days after day` (n's `received by the tenant on`)
    AND d AT LEAST o PLUS 1

-- s 64(3), note: "See also section 26B for an application a tenant may make to a competent court if the
-- tenant reasonably believes the lessor's action to terminate the residential tenancy agreement was
-- retaliatory action." A notice under s 64 is action to terminate (s 26A(a)(iii), REF-15, REF-22).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(3) note; s 26B(3)
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64(3), note -- the tenant given a s 64 notice may also apply under s 26B` r IF
        r's `action` EQUALS `action to terminate the agreement`
    AND `s 26B(3) -- the tenant may apply to a competent court for relief` r

§ `Section 65 -- Termination by lessor where s. 32 invoked`

-- Whether proceedings under s 32 are pending is a fact; whether an order under s 32 is in force on a day
-- is decided by s 32(5) (part-4-div-1-rent-and-bonds.l4), which the cases join to this rule.
DECLARE `Section 32 status` HAS
    `proceedings are pending for an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent is in force`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 65(1)
GIVEN s IS A `Section 32 status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65(1) -- the section bites` s IF
        s's `proceedings are pending for an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent`
    OR  s's `an order under s 32 fixing the maximum rent is in force`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 65(1)(a)
GIVEN s IS A `Section 32 status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65(1)(a) -- a notice of termination under s 64 is ineffectual` s IF
    `s 65(1) -- the section bites` s

-- s 65(1)(b): any other notice of termination by the lessor (including one under s 70A, REF-68, or on a
-- ground, REF-69) is ineffectual unless first authorised by a competent court under (2).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 65(1)(b)
GIVEN s IS A `Section 32 status`, `first authorised by a court under s 65(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65(1)(b) -- another notice of termination by the lessor is ineffectual` s `, authorised:` `first authorised by a court under s 65(2)` IF
        `s 65(1) -- the section bites` s
    AND NOT `first authorised by a court under s 65(2)`

-- s 65(2): the court may authorise the notice if satisfied that neither the proceedings nor the order
-- has wholly or partly motivated the lessor to give it.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 65(2)
GIVEN `the proceedings or the order wholly or partly motivated the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65(2) -- the court may authorise the notice, motivated:` `the proceedings or the order wholly or partly motivated the notice` IF
    NOT `the proceedings or the order wholly or partly motivated the notice`

§ `Section 70 -- Effect of notice of termination of periodic tenancy`

DECLARE `Objection to a notice ending a periodic tenancy` IS ONE OF
    `the period is shorter than the general law would require, though not shorter than the Act requires`
    `the day specified is not the last day of a period of the tenancy`
    `the period is shorter than the Act requires`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70(a), (b)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, o IS AN `Objection to a notice ending a periodic tenancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 70 -- the notice ending` a `is not ineffectual by reason of` o IF
        "Notice of termination of a residential tenancy agreement that creates a periodic tenancy"
    ... a's `kind` EQUALS `a periodic tenancy`
    AND (   "(a)" ... o EQUALS `the period is shorter than the general law would require, though not shorter than the Act requires`
         OR "(b)" ... o EQUALS `the day specified is not the last day of a period of the tenancy`)
